\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.  If Jehovah does not come to build the house\cf0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj The builders work will only be in vain
\par And if Jehovah does not guard the city
\par The watchman's work will only be in vain
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Fruitlessly do you get up early morning
\par And you sit down and are saddled with thoughts
\par You feed yourselves with pestilent and  troubles
\par But for those whom He loves, they rest in peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Behold, Jehovah's real treasures are children
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Fruits of the womb surely is a reward
\par Just as weapons are seen in the hands of giants
\par So are the children in the youthful age
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Blessed is the one who has his arrow sack
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Filled up to the brim, full, and in good hope
\par As for them, they will put nobody to shame
\par \pard    With enemies, they speak in city gate. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

